---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';

const schema = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: 'Terms of Service',
    url: new URL('/terms', SITE.url).href,
    description:
      'The terms for using ihateaudio.com and the iHateAudio app in ChatGPT: free, no account, your files stay yours.',
    publisher: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#organization` },
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'All tools', item: SITE.url },
      {
        '@type': 'ListItem',
        position: 2,
        name: 'Terms of Service',
        item: new URL('/terms', SITE.url).href,
      },
    ],
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Service and Fair Use"
  description="The terms for using ihateaudio.com and the iHateAudio app in ChatGPT. Free, no account, and your files stay yours."
  path="/terms"
  schema={schema}
>
  <div class="wrap page prose">
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="toolhead__sub" style="margin-bottom: var(--s8)">
      The short version: the tools are free, your files stay yours, and the
      tools come with no guarantee, so keep your originals.
    </p>

    <h2>Who runs this</h2>
    <p>
      iHateAudio is ihateaudio.com and the iHateAudio app in ChatGPT. Both are
      run by Harsh Manwani. In these terms, "we" and "us" mean that. By using
      either one, you agree to these terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Using the tools</h2>
    <p>
      Every tool is free and needs no account. You can use them for personal
      or commercial work.
    </p>

    <h2>Your files</h2>
    <p>
      You keep every right to the audio you bring and to what you make from it.
      We claim nothing in either. You are responsible for having the right to
      edit the audio you use.
    </p>
    <p>
      On the website, your files never leave your device. In ChatGPT, they are
      processed on our server and then deleted. The
      <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a> explains both.
    </p>

    <h2>Fair use of the ChatGPT app</h2>
    <p>
      Every job in the ChatGPT app runs on servers we pay for. Do not call it
      from scripts or anything other than ChatGPT, do not send it more work than
      a person would, and do not try to break it or reach anything behind it.
      We can limit or block use that harms the service or other people using
      it.
    </p>

    <h2>No guarantee</h2>
    <p>
      The tools are provided as they are, with no warranty of any kind. They can
      make mistakes: an AI tool can separate a voice badly, a transcript can
      mishear a word, and a tempo or key reading can be wrong. Check the result
      before you rely on it, and keep your original files.
    </p>
    <p>
      To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for any loss that comes
      from using iHateAudio, including lost files, lost work and lost income.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We can change these terms. The date below shows the current version, and
      using iHateAudio after a change means you accept it.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms go to
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <p><small>Last updated 4 October 2026.</small></p>
  </div>
</Base>
